# Auto-generated files — collapse diffs and exclude from language stats
web/package-lock.json linguist-generated=true

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# GENERATED FILES — REGENERATE, NEVER MERGE.
#
# `merge=union` and hand-resolution both produce a file that is valid but
# describes neither side. Both of these bit the v2026.7.20 merge:
#
#   uv.lock                        resolved by hand -> pytest-asyncio silently
#                                  went missing, and 321 of 419 failing test
#                                  files traced back to that one omission
#   website/static/api/model-catalog.json
#                                  taken from upstream wholesale -> it then
#                                  described UPSTREAM's model lists, not ours
#                                  (tencent/hy3 lost its "recommended" mark)
#
# `merge=ours` keeps our copy so the merge does not stall, then you MUST rerun
# the generator — the test suite checks both:
#   uv lock
#   python scripts/build_model_catalog.py
# See tasks/upstream-merge-hygiene.md.
#
# NOTE: `merge=ours` needs the driver registered once per clone (it is not a
# built-in). scripts/setup-merge-drivers.sh does it:
#   git config merge.ours.driver true
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
uv.lock                               merge=ours linguist-generated=true
website/static/api/model-catalog.json merge=ours linguist-generated=true

# Enforce LF for scripts that run inside Linux containers.
# Without this, Windows checkout converts to CRLF and breaks `exec` in the
# container entrypoint with "no such file or directory".
*.sh        text eol=lf
Dockerfile  text eol=lf
*.dockerfile text eol=lf
docker/entrypoint.sh text eol=lf
